  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A HIGH output (1) results only if all the inputs to the AND gate are HIGH (1). If not all inputs to the AND gate are HIGH, LOW output results.</p><p>But in case of OR Gate, for&nbsp;the output to be 1, at least input one OR two must be 1.</p><p>NOR Gate&nbsp;reverses the logic state.</p><p>Therefore, for all possible combination of inputs, outputs at different stages will look like as given below.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0068_a3c0302c948a.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 157px;\" /></p>"
